WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:02.350
What is a mirror?

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:06.129
Speaking in strictly literal terms, it’s
a reflective pane of glass that we use to

00:00:06.129 --> 00:00:09.330
check our hair or the clothes we’ve decided
to wear.

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:12.099
Seriously, how did you match that shirt with
those pants?

00:00:12.099 --> 00:00:15.669
But think about it another way, what is a
mirror for?

00:00:15.669 --> 00:00:20.480
Well, it’s for showing us ourselves, allowing
us to see what everybody else around us does

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:22.180
when they look in our direction.

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:25.400
In that way, you could say that a mirror is
honest.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:30.260
A mirror doesn’t lie, but that doesn't mean
they can’t hold secrets behind that looking

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:31.260
glass.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:37.010
Also known by the alternate name of the Red
Sea Object, SCP-093 is not a mirror itself,

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:40.820
it’s actually a red disc that has been carved
from cinnabar.

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:46.039
Cinnabar, for anyone not already aware, is
a toxic ore of mercury, that has been crafted

00:00:46.039 --> 00:00:50.610
into jewelry and ornaments in many parts of
the world over the centuries, thanks to its

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:52.539
ruby-like red coloration.

00:00:52.539 --> 00:00:59.269
The SCP-093 disc itself is only around 7.62
cm in diameter, fitting comfortably in most

00:00:59.269 --> 00:01:01.129
average-sized palms.

00:01:01.129 --> 00:01:05.430
All around the object are a number of symbols
carved into its surface, strange circular

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:08.120
engravings of unknown origin.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:12.340
The color of the red stone disc will also
apparently change based on whatever regrets

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:15.140
are being carried by the person who holds
it.

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:19.330
There seems to be some link between color
changes and the mental state or level of knowledge

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:21.090
possessed by the subject.

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:26.160
To put it in much simpler terms, think of
SCP-093’s color like one of those novelty

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:31.410
mood rings you see in gift shops, that change
to different hues supposedly to match a person’s

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:35.760
mood - although in actuality, it’s normally
changed by their body heat.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:41.200
The same cannot be said of the Red Sea Object:
It is stunningly accurate in peering into

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:44.750
your soul and diagnosing the darkness within.

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:49.320
If ever you come into contact with this baby,
you might even discover that it knows you

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:50.520
better than you.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:54.670
So, a weird, stone disc, doesn’t sound all
that impressive, does it?

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:57.300
And what does that have to do with mirrors?

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:04.350
Well, SCP-093 happens to have a certain attachment
to mirrors, and we mean that very, very literally.

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:08.769
If the Red Sea Object is ever not in front
of a mirror, or not being held by someone,

00:02:08.769 --> 00:02:12.349
it will speed towards the closest reflective
surface.

00:02:12.349 --> 00:02:18.159
As it rolls its way in the direction of the
nearest mirror, or mirror-like surface, SCP-093

00:02:18.159 --> 00:02:22.959
is capable of building up phenomenal speeds,
although curiously it never appears to cause

00:02:22.959 --> 00:02:28.069
any impact damage when it finally arrives,
neither to itself nor the mirror it latches

00:02:28.069 --> 00:02:29.099
on to.

00:02:29.099 --> 00:02:35.010
Which brings us to the next inevitable question,
what happens when SCP-093 is placed on or

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:37.040
attaches itself to a mirror?

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:40.830
Does it create a copy of the person who last
touched it, a clone that reflects all the

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:43.109
darkest parts of someone’s personality?

00:02:43.109 --> 00:02:48.650
Maybe it can allow the holder of SCP-093 to
themselves become like a mirror, bending light

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:52.020
away from their body in order to become functionally
invisible?

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:54.830
Well, it’s actually neither of these.

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:57.910
The truth is far more strange and existential.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:02.879
During extensive testing, the SCP Foundation
investigated the potential anomalous uses

00:03:02.879 --> 00:03:08.640
for SCP-093, paying especially close attention
to how the Red Sea Object interacted with

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:09.640
mirrors.

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:13.239
After a number of unsuccessful tests, they
finally learned what happens when someone

00:03:13.239 --> 00:03:17.719
places the disk onto a mirror: they move into
the mirror.

00:03:17.719 --> 00:03:22.909
Any mirror that SCP-093 is placed against
or otherwise attaches itself to is transformed

00:03:22.909 --> 00:03:26.109
into a portal of anomalous origin and destination.

00:03:26.109 --> 00:03:31.040
Naturally, the first instinct of the Foundation
personnel examining this artifact is to send

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:34.989
through an expedition to explore the other
side of this newly-formed mirror portal.

00:03:34.989 --> 00:03:37.129
So, that’s what they did.

00:03:37.129 --> 00:03:40.959
They gathered up a member of D-Class, the
imprisoned criminals that the Foundation uses

00:03:40.959 --> 00:03:43.999
as expendable subjects for dangerous tests.

00:03:43.999 --> 00:03:49.489
The subject was given water, ready to eat
meals, a flashlight, a gun, and a concealed

00:03:49.489 --> 00:03:52.769
knife, the latter of which the D-Class was
not made aware of.

00:03:52.769 --> 00:03:57.519
The first subject, despite having a past of
murder and attempted suicide, seemed to regret

00:03:57.519 --> 00:04:04.139
his actions and willingly agreed to cooperate
with testing, and as a result, SCP-093 emitted

00:04:04.139 --> 00:04:07.249
a blue glow, that also tinted the view in
the mirror.

00:04:07.249 --> 00:04:11.939
Perhaps, on the other side, he expected to
meet his end, and expected it as a righteous

00:04:11.939 --> 00:04:14.189
punishment for his life of sin.

00:04:14.189 --> 00:04:17.590
Stepping through the mirror, to the other
side of the looking glass, the D-Class found

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:23.259
himself in an empty field, not another person
or even a single tree in sight.

00:04:23.259 --> 00:04:27.979
Traversing forwards, he quickly came across
a section of grass that was barren, wilted,

00:04:27.979 --> 00:04:31.069
and dying, in the center of which was a hole.

00:04:31.069 --> 00:04:35.550
Climbing in as per Foundation instructions,
the man found only dirt for about a hundred

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:36.550
meters.

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:38.520
But then, something strange happened.

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:42.660
The dirt around him gradually gave way to
a concrete enclosure that the man remarked

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:44.690
stank of something awful.

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:49.569
The room was lit by a series of ceiling light
fixtures, some of which were already broken.

00:04:49.569 --> 00:04:53.780
Three doors were positioned on either side
of the enclosure, with an extra door at the

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:57.300
far end, blocked by some fallen metal shelving.

00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:01.610
The existence of a place like this seemed
to imply that someone, was present beyond

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:02.610
the portal.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:05.050
Or at least, they had been.

00:05:05.050 --> 00:05:09.639
This ancient underground bunker, lost to time,
seemed to have traces that people had once

00:05:09.639 --> 00:05:10.660
lived there.

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:15.560
In one of the adjacent rooms, the ceiling
seemed to be coated in a smelly, brown sludge.

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:19.629
But it was in here that the D-Class discovered
a makeshift cot, wooden crates containing

00:05:19.629 --> 00:05:24.370
foodstuffs and empty water bottles, and a
book lying next to the cot.

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:28.690
When he attempted to approach the book, he
was assaulted by a screeching noise like grinding

00:05:28.690 --> 00:05:29.690
metal.

00:05:29.690 --> 00:05:31.509
The door was beginning to close.

00:05:31.509 --> 00:05:36.090
As the D-Class dashed out, the bodycam he’d
been fitted with seemed to pick up a figure,

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:39.350
standing at the end of the corridor where
the seventh door was.

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:45.050
It opened the door from behind, just a crack,
looked in, and silently shut it once more.

00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:49.479
Finding only crumpled newspapers and food
rations, the Foundation ordered the intrepid

00:05:49.479 --> 00:05:51.380
D-Class to return to the mirror.

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:56.030
Suddenly, something tugged at the lifeline
secured around his waist; something was pulling

00:05:56.030 --> 00:05:57.490
him up out of the tunnel.

00:05:57.490 --> 00:06:01.190
While trying to get back to the mirror, the
D-Class witnessed a group of thirty-seven

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:05.940
figures, all of them faceless, with no discernible
features to speak of.

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:09.990
In his escape, he opened fire with the gun
he’d been issued, but not at the crowd,

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:11.460
at something bigger.

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:16.319
A massive humanoid creature, around fifty
times bigger than an average person, was crawling

00:06:16.319 --> 00:06:18.220
around on the ground.

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:22.889
Like the other figures, this giant was without
a face, pulling itself towards the mirror

00:06:22.889 --> 00:06:27.009
as the D-Class was reeled back through the
mirror by a cable and pulley.

00:06:27.009 --> 00:06:32.430
After their first glimpse into the world within
SCP-093, naturally, the Foundation were curious

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:33.680
to learn more.

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:38.360
The next test revealed more about this other
reality, for one, that the Red Sea Object

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:42.960
seemed to choose its locations based on the
personal history of whoever was traveling

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:44.199
through a mirror.

00:06:44.199 --> 00:06:49.259
This time, it was a female D-Class, who had
killed two children whilst stealing a car.

00:06:49.259 --> 00:06:53.699
She arrived at a farmhouse, which had a bunker
of its own, like the first test.

00:06:53.699 --> 00:06:57.819
Much like then, there were definite signs
that someone had inhabited the bunker before

00:06:57.819 --> 00:07:03.050
her arrival, but most telling were the three
skeletons and empty revolver.

00:07:03.050 --> 00:07:07.430
It seems that everyone in this world lived
in bunkers at some point, possibly to hide

00:07:07.430 --> 00:07:10.599
from the various faceless creatures that roam
the landscape.

00:07:10.599 --> 00:07:14.710
Additionally, any remnants of a civilization
that were uncovered seemed to fit the aesthetic

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:19.870
of the 1950s, however, this civilization also
seemed to have technology comparable to that

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:21.960
found in the 21st century.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:26.580
The D-Class discovered a laptop, the casing
of which also seemed to resemble a fifties

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:27.580
style.

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:31.289
Booting the machine up revealed the final
moments of its operating system, something

00:07:31.289 --> 00:07:34.120
called “Faithful OS.”

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:38.159
Instances of the same operating system seemed
to crop up everywhere the more the Foundation

00:07:38.159 --> 00:07:40.430
sent expeditions through the mirrors.

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:46.610
The world that SCP-093 had offered access
to seemed to be brimming with advanced technology,

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:51.160
far more impressive inventions than anything
that exists in our world.

00:07:51.160 --> 00:07:56.010
Not just computers either, but this world
even had functional self-driving cars!

00:07:56.010 --> 00:07:57.550
Suck on that, Elon Musk!

00:07:57.550 --> 00:08:04.509
And yet, even with all that advancement, they
were still stuck in the fifties, 1953 to be

00:08:04.509 --> 00:08:09.259
exact, as one expedition discovered that was
the last recorded year of this world.

00:08:09.259 --> 00:08:13.960
But something had clearly occurred here, some
sort of devastating event that had wiped out

00:08:13.960 --> 00:08:19.319
almost all of humanity and driven the survivors
into underground bunkers where they eventually

00:08:19.319 --> 00:08:20.319
perished.

00:08:20.319 --> 00:08:21.319
But what?

00:08:21.319 --> 00:08:23.319
The sudden arrival of those faceless creatures?

00:08:23.319 --> 00:08:27.780
Or was it more to do with that strange, viscous
brown sludge that seemed to be cropping up

00:08:27.780 --> 00:08:29.370
all over the place?

00:08:29.370 --> 00:08:34.099
This world seemed to be abundant with religious
imagery, even down to the naming of Faithful

00:08:34.099 --> 00:08:35.450
OS.

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:39.519
Symbols of hands clasped together in prayer
and other iconography linked to Christianity

00:08:39.519 --> 00:08:44.440
could be found everywhere, from the outer
sides of buildings, to the computers and folders

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:49.070
found when the Foundation expeditions delved
deeper into the cities and offices.

00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:53.280
In one, they discovered a waiting area assumed
to be connected to a doctor’s office, which

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:57.060
provided more clues as to just what had happened
here.

00:08:57.060 --> 00:09:00.240
Examining the contents of the receptionist’s
computer in this office revealed that the

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:04.889
doctors of this world were deeply ingrained
in theology, and were responsible for treating

00:09:04.889 --> 00:09:07.800
their patients for a number of strange symptoms.

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:12.790
One entry described a woman, ‘Citizen Jennifer
McZirka’, who seemingly suffered ‘a lapse

00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:13.970
of the heart’.

00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:18.170
This apparent condition caused her to sin,
committing adultery before she was admitted

00:09:18.170 --> 00:09:21.860
“into the Lord's and our hands for cleansing
of mind and body.”

00:09:21.860 --> 00:09:26.500
It appeared that this world took religion
to an extreme, employing doctors to cure sinners

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:31.860
of their trespasses through the use of something
referred to as ‘The Lord’s Tears’; that

00:09:31.860 --> 00:09:35.250
brown fluid splattered all over this mirror
world.

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:40.090
This substance, as the Foundation soon learned,
was harvested from the giant faceless creatures

00:09:40.090 --> 00:09:45.279
that roamed freely around this place, but
the question still remained: why?

00:09:45.279 --> 00:09:50.140
The answers were uncovered in another expedition,
this time by a Foundation service technician

00:09:50.140 --> 00:09:55.520
who was able to make SCP-093 turn a bright
red color when he affixed it to a mirror.

00:09:55.520 --> 00:10:00.850
He was transported to a room with a rotating
pillar, with beams of light that shone upon…

00:10:00.850 --> 00:10:04.209
other copies of SCP-093.

00:10:04.209 --> 00:10:08.889
These various copies of the mirror portal
system seemed to be leading to other mysterious

00:10:08.889 --> 00:10:09.889
worlds.

00:10:09.889 --> 00:10:13.830
As if looking back behind the curtain, the
technician found an adjacent room filled with

00:10:13.830 --> 00:10:18.970
computer equipment, monitoring these other
worlds, and categorizing them as either ‘Clean’,

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:20.620
‘Unclean’ or ‘Lost’.

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:22.490
So, what do we have?

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:25.350
Where does all of this leave us besides scratching
our heads?

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:29.899
Clearly, some sort of cataclysmic disaster
occurred in one of these mirror worlds.

00:10:29.899 --> 00:10:34.370
It had once been a place where technology
had boomed in the 1950s, but that was also

00:10:34.370 --> 00:10:38.740
steeped in deep religious beliefs, to the
extent where sinners were treated with a strange

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:41.959
substance extracted from those faceless creatures.

00:10:41.959 --> 00:10:47.389
It seems as if some time ago, a god-like being
known only as Him, arrived in one of these

00:10:47.389 --> 00:10:51.870
worlds and this served as the catalyst for
such an advancement in technology.

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:57.100
However, He had also deemed this world to
be Unclean and full of sin, mandating a purge

00:10:57.100 --> 00:10:59.930
of all sinners in order to cleanse the world.

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:04.519
As a result, a holy war took place to determine
who was worthy of salvation.

00:11:04.519 --> 00:11:09.430
A deeply religious society formed around the
arrival of Him, and their primary weapon against

00:11:09.430 --> 00:11:13.670
the sinners was the brown liquid, His Holy
Tears.

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:15.760
And those monsters prowling around?

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:19.800
One part of the Unclean, their Sins given
form.

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:21.459
Except none of that was true.

00:11:21.459 --> 00:11:26.130
There never was a war, no fight between holiness
and cleanliness.

00:11:26.130 --> 00:11:31.079
The truth was this being, this eldritch abomination
had arrived to conquer.

00:11:31.079 --> 00:11:37.519
Using the disks, like SCP-093, he traveled
to that world, fed them lies, and turned the

00:11:37.519 --> 00:11:43.600
people into his followers, becoming the master
of their world and eventually its destroyer.

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:49.350
Ultimately, SCP-093 is a warning, a look at
what happens when a being like this takes

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:50.350
over.

00:11:50.350 --> 00:11:56.199
The broken, dead world that the Red Sea Object
transports us to is a legacy of His destruction,

00:11:56.199 --> 00:12:01.290
a false god preying on humanity and their
beliefs like a theological predator.

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:06.620
Then, when His work is done, He moves on to
find a new world to conquer.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:11.730
We can only hope that his gaze never rests
upon ours, or that what the Red Sea Object

00:12:11.730 --> 00:12:15.920
knows of our many sins will be the least of
our problems.

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:21.730
Now go check out “SCP-2317 - The Devourer
of Worlds / A Door to Another World” and

00:12:21.730 --> 00:12:27.209
“SCP-001 - The Black Moon” for more monsters
we definitely don’t want to enter our dimension!

